From 016118faafdf3b4ec95af7dcac24ff3f78c8a9c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:15:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] ksmbd: require exact EA name matches

smb2_get_ea() uses the request's EaNameLength as the length of a
strncmp() against each eligible user xattr name without first requiring
the candidate name to have the same length.  A request for "foo" can
therefore match "user.foobar" and return the name and value of a
different EA.

Require the xattr name to contain exactly the "user." prefix followed by
EaNameLength bytes before comparing the requested bytes.  Compare exactly
EaNameLength bytes with memcmp(); EaNameLength excludes the required
terminating NUL.

Reachable over the network from an authenticated client:

  SMB2 QUERY_INFO
    -> smb2_query_info()
    -> SMB2_O_INFO_FILE -> smb2_get_info_file()
    -> FILE_FULL_EA_INFORMATION -> smb2_get_ea()
    -> ksmbd_vfs_listxattr(), then strncmp(EaNameLength) per eligible EA

Preconditions: a valid FileId, a handle carrying FILE_READ_EA, and a
file holding an eligible, non-internal user.* xattr whose name extends
the requested prefix.  The request bounds checks ensure that
EaNameLength name bytes are present, so memcmp() cannot read out of
bounds.

Signed-off-by: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
Reviewed-by: ChenXiaoSong <chenxiaosong@kylinos.cn>
---
 fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
index 76f63f9adc72..220d5850f96c 100644
--- a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
@@ -5206,8 +5206,9 @@ static int smb2_get_ea(struct ksmbd_work *work, struct ksmbd_file *fp,
 			continue;
 
 		if (req->InputBufferLength &&
-		    strncmp(&name[XATTR_USER_PREFIX_LEN], ea_req->name,
-			    ea_req->EaNameLength))
+		    (name_len != XATTR_USER_PREFIX_LEN + ea_req->EaNameLength ||
+		     memcmp(&name[XATTR_USER_PREFIX_LEN], ea_req->name,
+			    ea_req->EaNameLength)))
 			continue;
 
 		if (!strncmp(&name[XATTR_USER_PREFIX_LEN],
-- 
